    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.5,
      "end_seconds": 260.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "nearly finished here"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.51,
      "end_seconds": 282.16,
      "duration_seconds": 10.65,
      "text": "there is pain when you lift the arm out to the side between about sixty and one hundred and twenty degrees, and the grip strength is normal"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.64,
      "end_seconds": 289.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "All finished thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 305.83,
      "end_seconds": 336.55,
      "duration_seconds": 30.72,
      "text": "from what you've told me and what I found it points towards a rotator cuff tendon problem the reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. Neck-related arm pain is still possible let's book a shoulder X-ray to look into shoulder pain that will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step i'm going to order an ultrasound of the shoulder for shoulder pain"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 338.54,
      "end_seconds": 364.44,
      "duration_seconds": 25.9,
      "text": "I'm gonna put you on naproxen 250 milligrams twice a day with food for one week. That should help with shoulder pain. Keep the shoulder moving gently within comfort and avoid heavy overhead lifting. A short walk every day even twenty minutes will help more than you'd think. I'd like you to see physiotherapy as well and I'll write the referral."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 366.05,
      "end_seconds": 374.86,
      "duration_seconds": 8.81,
      "text": "One warning sign to remember: the arm becomes numb or you get fever. In that case don't wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 376.22,
      "end_seconds": 378.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "Thank you, that's clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 380.23,
      "end_seconds": 382.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
